# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Docker / ngrok settings for the Equb admin panel.
#
#  Copy the lines you need into your existing .env — docker compose reads
#  ./.env automatically, so there is no second file to keep in sync and no
#  --env-file flag to remember. Everything here has a working default; this
#  file exists to document the knobs, not to be required.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Already in .env; repeated here because the image BAKES them ─────────────
# Next.js inlines every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value at BUILD time, so changing one of
# these needs `docker compose up -d --build`, not a restart.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.emadssl.com/api/v1/
# NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCK=false
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENFORCE_PERMS=

# ── Runtime only ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read per request by src/app/api/backend/[...path]/route.ts, the server-side
# proxy the browser falls back to. A restart is enough to change it.
# Leave unset unless the server should reach the backend at a different address
# than the browser does (e.g. an internal host); unset falls back to the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL baked into the image.
# BACKEND_API_BASE_URL=http://backend:8080/api/v1

# ── Ports ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4100 keeps clear of the Sacco frontend, which owns 4000 on these machines.
# WEB_PORT=4100
# NGROK_INSPECT_PORT=4140

# ── ngrok ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for `docker compose --profile tunnel up -d`, and for nothing else.
# Get it from https://dashboard.ngrok.com/get-started/your-authtoken
# NGROK_AUTHTOKEN=

# Build-time npm registry. Switch to https://registry.npmmirror.com if npmjs
# is slow or blocked on your connection.
# PNPM_REGISTRY=https://registry.npmjs.org
